  "question": {
    "text": "The line \\(a x+b y=1\\) cuts ellipse \\(c x^2+d y^2=1\\) only once if",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "twjDD",
      "text": "\\(\\mathrm{ca}^2+\\mathrm{db}^2=1\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "drOCG",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{c}}{\\mathrm{a}^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{b}^2}=1\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wO5zU",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{a}^2}{\\mathrm{c}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{\\mathrm{~d}}=1\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dXdXE",
      "text": "\\(a c^2+b d^2=1\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Clearly \\(a x+b y=1\\)\ni.e \\(y=-\\frac{a}{b} x+\\frac{1}{b}\\) is tangent to\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{cx}^2+\\mathrm{dy}^2=1 \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{\\frac{1}{c}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{\\frac{1}{d}}=1 \\\\\n& \\therefore\\left(\\frac{1}{b}\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{1}{c}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{a}{b}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{d}\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 1=\\frac{a^2}{c}+\\frac{b^2}{d}\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
